{"apikey":"api2demo","success":true,"requestNumber":999,"itemsCount":2,"totalResults":129621,"items":[{"completeness":10,"country":["Sweden"],"dataProvider":["Museum of Ethnography"],"dcCreator":["Mununggurr, Mutitjpuy, aboriginer","Mouthwatch, Mutitjpuy, Aborigines","Mununggurr, Mutitjpuy, aboriginer"],"dcCreatorLangAware":{"sv":["Mununggurr, Mutitjpuy, aboriginer"],"def":["Mununggurr, Mutitjpuy, aboriginer"],"en":["Mouthwatch, Mutitjpuy, Aborigines"]},"dcDescription":["1977.19.0003","\"Here is portrayed three Moods of the Sky and the effects on the Fish and Animals. Sharks and Turtles come to the Surface when it is Raining. Wallabies and Kangaroos are out feeding at first light when the Morning Star is brightest. Stars still shine although a quick Tropical Storm can produce lightening as seen from the Mouthes of the Snakes. \"Bapi\" is the name given for Lightening and Snakes.\" (Area Caledon to Blue Mud Bay. Artist: Mutitjpuy.","DSM, Australien [5]","Nya Holland","Australia","köp","utställd i DSM-Australien 1999 [[Mag]]","Den skapande människan","DSM, Australien [5]","Nya Holland","\"Here is portrayed three Moods of the Sky and the effects on the Fish and Animals. Sharks and Turtles come to the Surface when it is Raining. Wallabies and Kangaroos are out feeding at first light when the Morning Star is brightest. Stars still shine although a quick Tropical Storm can produce lightening as seen from the Mouthes of the Snakes. \"Bapi\" is the name given for Lightening and Snakes.\" (Area Caledon to Blue Mud Bay. Artist: Mutitjpuy.","Australia","1977.19.0003"],"dcDescriptionLangAware":{"sv":["köp","utställd i DSM-Australien 1999 [[Mag]]","Den skapande människan","DSM, Australien [5]","Nya Holland"],"def":["1977.19.0003","\"Here is portrayed three Moods of the Sky and the effects on the Fish and Animals. Sharks and Turtles come to the Surface when it is Raining. Wallabies and Kangaroos are out feeding at first light when the Morning Star is brightest. Stars still shine although a quick Tropical Storm can produce lightening as seen from the Mouthes of the Snakes. \"Bapi\" is the name given for Lightening and Snakes.\" (Area Caledon to Blue Mud Bay. Artist: Mutitjpuy.","DSM, Australien [5]","Nya Holland","Australia"],"en":["\"Here is portrayed three Moods of the Sky and the effects on the Fish and Animals. Sharks and Turtles come to the Surface when it is Raining. Wallabies and Kangaroos are out feeding at first light when the Morning Star is brightest. Stars still shine although a quick Tropical Storm can produce lightening as seen from the Mouthes of the Snakes. \"Bapi\" is the name given for Lightening and Snakes.\" (Area Caledon to Blue Mud Bay. Artist: Mutitjpuy.","Australia"],"zxx":["1977.19.0003"]},"dcLanguage":["sv","swe"],"dcLanguageLangAware":{"def":["sv","swe"]},"dcTitleLangAware":{"sv":["målning, barkmålning, painting"],"en":["painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting and painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting and painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting, painting and painting, painting, painting, painting, painti